<p>(a)  On Nov. 15, 1995, World Trade Bank was acquired and accounted for as a purchase.  Fair value of assets acquired was $40.7 million.  346,325 shares of bank common stock were issued. Rights offering to all shareholders of record of the Bank's common stock as of Oct. 24, 1995, was closed Nov. 30, 1995. 651,325 shares of bank common stock were issued.</p>
<p>(b)  In the third quarter 1996, the bank was assessed by the Federal Deposit Insurance Corp. $132,000 to fund the Savings Association Insurance Fund.  This was a one-time assessment. Earnings per share would have been 5 cents in the third quarter of 1996 without the assessment.</p>
<p>(c)  No provision for income tax expense has been recognized due to federal and state net operating loss of prior years carried forward to offset income of reported period.</p>
<p>(d)  At Dec. 31, 1996, 690,336 warrants were issued and outstanding that allow the holder to purchase one share of the bank's common stock for $3.75.  These warrants expire on Dec. 1, 1998. At Dec. 31, 1996, the bank had 125,336 shares under option, of which 115,300 allow the holder to purchase one share of the bank's common stock for $4. In determining earnings per share, the bank uses the treasury stock method, which assumes that the holders of the warrants and options purchase the bank's common stock and the proceeds are used by the bank to repurchase those shares at the reporting period's average common stock security price.  The difference between warrants and options outstanding and the potential options and warrants purchased by the bank are added to common shares outstanding.</p>
<p>(e)  Financial ratio for quarters is based on an annualized net income.</p>
<p>(f)  Noninterest expense to interest income and noninterest income.</p>
